# The brotli bytes a first visit downloads for each wasm module the web app ships, at most, by the
# Nix system that builds it: each module is `packages.${system}`'s, and an aarch64 build of the
# same revision is not byte for byte an x86_64 one (typst-wasm: 6,276,915 bytes brotli on
# aarch64-linux, 6,271,632 on x86_64-linux, each reproduced by `nix build --rebuild`). Each line is
# its system's figure, as `nix build` and build-web.sh's `brotli -q 11` make it, rounded up to a
# thousand bytes so a change that moves a module by less need not move its line.
# scripts/build-web.sh refuses a module over its system's line, or one with no line. A line only
# moves down: app/cli/tests/guards/wasm_budget.rs refuses one raised against the merge base.
#
# <module> <system> <bytes>
# Stages 7 and 8 (#341) raise views_bg and prodrome_bg: the todo list, a todo and the Typst list in
# the pages' module, and the list's tree grown in the core's. x86_64 is measured; aarch64 is x86_64
# plus the gap master's lines kept, until an aarch64 build of the merge measures it.
# localwrites stage 1 (#462) raises prodrome_bg by the asks store's replica and the topic stores'
# signing and refusals, measured as +22,117 bytes brotli before wasm-opt on x86_64.
views_bg.wasm x86_64-linux 615000
prodrome_bg.wasm x86_64-linux 1152000
typst_bg.wasm x86_64-linux 6272000
views_bg.wasm aarch64-linux 622000
prodrome_bg.wasm aarch64-linux 1166000
typst_bg.wasm aarch64-linux 6277000
